      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MV H3\n\nSong + isolated vocal + one photo → finished music video, joined and muxed.\nNo ffmpeg.\n\nOutput: `output/minimax_h3_t8_long_video/<chain_id>/assembled/*_master_audio.mp4`\n\nFull docs, model download links and the Claude Code skill:\n**github.com/oomsurvivor/comfyui-mv-autodirect**\n\n---\n\n**Vocal must be the isolated lead stem.** Backing vocals count as singing and\nbreak the timing.\n\n**Both `AudioCrop` nodes need the same `start_time` / `end_time`**, and\n`end_time` at least 1 second shorter than the shorter file. Otherwise:\n`resolves to N frames but requires M`.\n\n## Three ways to run\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Preview** | Ctrl+B on the renderer → Run → read `PreviewAny`. **No GPU, near-instant.** Change `seed` and repeat until the plan looks right. |\n| **Excerpt** | change `end_time` on **both** AudioCrops + new `chain_id` |\n| **Full song** | `0:00` → length minus 1–2 s + new `chain_id` |\n\nShort runs cost *more* per scene — the model reloads for every scene and that\nfixed cost is spread over fewer of them. Iterate with Preview, not with short\nrenders.\n\n## chain_id — the one real trap\n\nReusing a **finished** `chain_id` generates nothing and re-exports the old\nvideo in a second, with no error. Signs: no `100%|███ 6/6` bar, GPU quiet.\n\n**New look → new chain_id.**\n\n## The four fields on MV Auto Director\n\nIn the order they appear: `custom_global_prompt` (required) ·\n`custom_angles_json` · `custom_light` · `custom_pose`\n\nDescribe crowds in the **global** field only — it is not word-filtered, the\nangle library is. Lock the light to a fixed world position so cuts don't\nflicker.\n\n`busy_background`: leave on `auto`. It avoids pairing expensive moves with wide\nshots, which can take roughly ten times as long.\n\n`pose_scenes` / `pose_every` make scenes stop lip-syncing. A third is a good\nrhythm; put them at the intro, a breakdown, and after a chorus payoff.\n\n## Notes\n\n`accepted/` means the file landed, not that the frame is good. Check for a\nduplicated face or a second ball — a bad scene poisons every scene after it.\n\nClosing the **console** kills the server; closing the **browser tab** does not.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# MV H3\n\nSong + isolated vocal + one photo → finished music video, joined and muxed.\nNo ffmpeg.\n\nOutput: `output/minimax_h3_t8_long_video/<chain_id>/assembled/*_master_audio.mp4`\n\nFull docs, model download links and the Claude Code skill:\n**github.com/oomsurvivor/comfyui-mv-autodirect**\n\n---\n\n**Vocal must be the isolated lead stem.** Backing vocals count as singing and\nbreak the timing.\n\n**Both `AudioCrop` nodes need the same `start_time` / `end_time`**, and\n`end_time` at least 1 second shorter than the shorter file. Otherwise:\n`resolves to N frames but requires M`.\n\n## Three ways to run\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Preview** | Ctrl+B on the renderer → Run → read `PreviewAny`. **No GPU, near-instant.** Change `seed` and repeat until the plan looks right. |\n| **Excerpt** | change `end_time` on **both** AudioCrops + new `chain_id` |\n| **Full song** | `0:00` → length minus 1–2 s + new `chain_id` |\n\nShort runs cost *more* per scene — the model reloads for every scene and that\nfixed cost is spread over fewer of them. Iterate with Preview, not with short\nrenders.\n\n## chain_id — the one real trap\n\nReusing a **finished** `chain_id` generates nothing and re-exports the old\nvideo in a second, with no error. Signs: no `100%|███ 6/6` bar, GPU quiet.\n\n**New look → new chain_id.**\n\n## The four fields on MV Auto Director\n\nIn the order they appear: `custom_global_prompt` (required) ·\n`custom_angles_json` · `custom_light` · `custom_pose`\n\nDescribe crowds in the **global** field only — it is not word-filtered, the\nangle library is. Lock the light to a fixed world position so cuts don't\nflicker.\n\n`busy_background`: leave on `auto`. It avoids pairing expensive moves with wide\nshots, which can take roughly ten times as long.\n\n`pose_scenes` / `pose_every` make scenes stop lip-syncing. A third is a good\nrhythm; put them at the intro, a breakdown, and after a chorus payoff.\n\n## Notes\n\n`accepted/` means the file landed, not that the frame is good. Check for a\nduplicated face or a second ball — a bad scene poisons every scene after it.\n\nClosing the **console** kills the server; closing the **browser tab** does not.\n"
      },
      "color": "#1d4d3a",
      "bgcolor": "#102a20"
    },
